## Review gates
Review A correctness: applies in all three phases (lead).
Review B security: applies in Phase 2 only, narrow — TSV path traversal, 108 SHA-256 values, read-only handoff, no secret or private file staged, no Thai in outputs, video files out of git. Not applicable in Phase 1 or Phase 3.
Review C UX/API: applies in Phase 1 and Phase 2, narrow — CLI flags, defaults, exit codes, output paths, and pure layout and intake contracts. No route or page. Not applicable in Phase 3.
Adversarial: applies in Phase 1 and Phase 2, one focused round each (one-frame time shift, bubble overlap, missing manifest row, changed hash, missing cut-out, week 1 frame hashes). Not applicable in Phase 3.
UX browser: not applicable in all phases. No page, route, DOM, CSS, or interactive flow. Remotion studio is a viewing aid. Visual acceptance comes from decoded frame sheets and the Daniel or Storytime look check; week 1 was approved 2026-11-04.

